  "description": "<p>Issuing a purgeDatastream request with a malformed startDT (e.g. \"1999\") results in a 500 error when using FeSL AuthZ but a 400 error when using the legacy AuthZ.</p>\n\n<p>With the legacy AuthZ, DateUtility returns an IllegalArgumentException, which is eventually translated into a 400 (Bad request; unable to fulfill REST API request), e.g.:</p>\n\n<p>INFO 2012-08-30 16:25:56.150 <span class=\"error\">&#91;http-8080-1&#93;</span> (DefaultManagement) Completed getDatastream(pid: test-rest:1, datastreamID: testMalformedDates, asOfDateTime: null)<br/>\nWARN 2012-08-30 16:25:56.176 <span class=\"error\">&#91;http-8080-6&#93;</span> (BaseRestResource) Bad request; unable to fulfill REST API request<br/>\njava.lang.IllegalArgumentException: Unparseable date: \"1999\"<br/>\n\tat org.fcrepo.utilities.DateUtility.parseDateOrNull(DateUtility.java:210) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;fcrepo-common-3.6.1-SNAPSHOT.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n\tat org.fcrepo.server.rest.DatastreamResource.deleteDatastream(DatastreamResource.java:286) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;fcrepo-server-3.6.1-SNAPSHOT.jar:na&#93;</span></p>\n\n<p>However, with FeSL AuthZ, the date parsing is done by the xacml library which results in a ParseException that eventually translates into in a 500, e.g.:</p>\n\n<p>INFO 2012-08-30 16:41:07.482 <span class=\"error\">&#91;http-8080-6&#93;</span> (DefaultManagement) Completed getDatastream(pid: test-rest:1, datastreamID: testMalformedDates, asOfDateTime: null)<br/>\nERROR 2012-08-30 16:41:07.501 <span class=\"error\">&#91;http-8080-7&#93;</span> (PurgeDatastream) <br/>\njava.text.ParseException: <br/>\n\tat com.sun.xacml.attr.DateTimeAttribute.strictParse(DateTimeAttribute.java:413) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;sunxacml-1.2-melcoe.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n\tat com.sun.xacml.attr.DateTimeAttribute.getInstance(DateTimeAttribute.java:379) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;sunxacml-1.2-melcoe.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n\tat org.fcrepo.server.security.xacml.pep.rest.objectshandlers.PurgeDatastream.handleRequest(PurgeDatastream.java:108) ~<span class=\"error\">&#91;fcrepo-security-pep-3.6.1-SNAPSHOT.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n\tat org.fcrepo.server.security.xacml.pep.rest.PEP.doFilter(PEP.java:160) <span class=\"error\">&#91;fcrepo-security-pep-3.6.1-SNAPSHOT.jar:na&#93;</span></p>\n\n<p>We need to decide what is the appropriate response here and then be consistent about it.</p>",
